      "writtenOn": "2021-02-06T04:33:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As this is the big entry point, maybe we want to beef up the documentation with :\n• Details what it does exactly. Try to describe it in the light of concrete automotive use cases, rather than a generic mechanism to direct app traffic to any desired network (in an effort to avoid attracting attention from parties looking to violate network neutrality and user privacy)\n• One example of typical usage, to support the explanation\n• A description of error modes (what can be thrown, what errors come through the listener)\n• Guarantees of listener calls (e.g. the listener is guaranteed to be called exactly once, unless security exception is thrown or something)",
