      "writtenOn": "2021-02-06T04:33:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Catching NPE is really a niche case – why specifically do you need to do this here ?\n\nIt may be reasonable to want to never throw and always report errors through the listener, but then you want to catch Exception instead.\nAlso, usually we do have at least some exceptions that can just be thrown synchronously from this kind of method. SecurityException is a good example of these – any party trying to call this without appropriate permisions should be sent SE synchronously. NPE, if in a reaction to an illegal null argument, is another common thing (this is already what the current patchset is doing as l.9326 will behave like this).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9335,
        "startChar": 47,
        "endLine": 9335,
        "endChar": 67
      },
      "revId": "d5e8efc6efd8c2fc61d5fdbe0d63655e8887e79a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
