        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-06T04:33:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a bit baroque usage. I understand you can\u0027t just remotely pass any exception – the client may not have those classes in their app space. But if we have a good idea of what kind of errors we may send there, it is relatively common practice to have a short list of possible specific exceptions in the boot class path, and make the listener take an exception as an argument. If you choose to do so, you need to\n• Have a short list of exceptions that can be thrown, and describe them in documentation\n• Possibly pass ServiceSpecificException with a message if you catch an exception you didn\u0027t expect",
